Pokemon Yellow Save Editor - Reference Data Sources
====================================================

This project's save-format knowledge and immutable data tables
(src/yellow_data.c, src/yellow.c offsets and algorithms) were derived
from the following sources. PKHeX was consulted for format facts and
Yellow-specific constants; its C# implementation is not included.
The base data tables come from kasbuunk/Pokemon, with its MIT notice
retained below. Pokemon is a trademark of Nintendo,
Creatures Inc., and GAME FREAK inc.; this project is an independent
fan-made tool and is not affiliated with or endorsed by them.

1. kasbuunk/Pokemon (MIT License)
   Repository: https://github.com/kasbuunk/Pokemon
   Pinned commit: ac72f04af1026b4023015c239b34730b8cccb15e
   (2026-07-18, "fix(storage): fit the center column into short
   viewports")
   Used: Gen 1 save layout (crates/pksave/src/gen1/offsets.rs, verified
   against pokered.sym), record structures (party.rs, pokemon.rs,
   boxes.rs, items.rs, trainer.rs, bcd.rs), checksum algorithm
   (checksum.rs), stat/experience formulas and growth-rate coefficients
   (stats.rs), text charmap (text.rs), and the generated species/move/
   item/type tables (data/generated/*.rs) that seed src/yellow_data.c.
   License text: see below ("kasbuunk/Pokemon MIT License").
   kasbuunk's tables are themselves generated from pret/pokered.

2. pret/pokered (no license file; unlicensed disassembly)
   Repository: https://github.com/pret/pokered
   Pinned commit: a1a22aaf84d1675bcdbaeb194592379d586d838e
   Used: constants/charmap.asm (English character encoding),
   engine/items/item_effects.asm AddBonusPP (the PP Up bonus formula:
   each PP Up adds min(7, floor(base_pp / 5))), data/growth_rates.asm
   coefficients (via the kasbuunk tables), wPlayerStarter semantics.
   pokered carries no license; only factual constants and formulas
   were referenced, and no pokered source text is included here.

3. pret/pokeyellow (no license file; unlicensed disassembly)
   Repository: https://github.com/pret/pokeyellow
   Pinned commit: e89ead154b9968aa50eed9328ff2b38b6c194382
   Used: cross-check of base stats against Yellow.

4. kwsch/PKHeX (GPL-3.0; format/data reference)
   Repository: https://github.com/kwsch/PKHeX
   Pinned commit: e0e63bc87837ad2d9c8f8fda4efdbf5f2933db08
   (2026-09-06, "Minor tweaks")
   Used: PKHeX.Core/Resources/byte/personal/personal_y (binary
   PersonalTable.Y) to obtain the four Yellow-specific catch rates that
   differ from Red/Blue: Pikachu 163 (vs 190), Kadabra 96 (vs 100),
   Dragonair 27 (vs 45), Dragonite 9 (vs 45); and
   Legality/Encounters/Templates/Gen1/EncounterStatic1.cs
   (LightBallPikachuCatchRate = 163) as corroboration. Read-only
   reference: no PKHeX code is included in this project.
   ItemStorage1.General also informed the allowed bag item IDs.

Regeneration
------------
tools/generate_yellow_data.py regenerates src/yellow_data.c from the
pinned kasbuunk/Pokemon checkout and the PKHeX
personal_y blob for the four Yellow catch-rate overrides. Run it from
the repository root with the reference checkouts available; the
generator records the same pinned commits in its output header.

5. X7 SD transport and filesystem
   src/x7_disk.c derives from untoxa/VGM_player (Copyright 2024 Toxa,
   MIT; full license in vendor/petitfatfs/DRIVER-LICENSE), with the
   SD write path and FatFs integration reused from the local
   modretro-chromatic project. FatFs R0.16 includes official patches
   1 and 2; see vendor/fatfs/LICENSE.txt and provenance.json.

